## Context
Child of tracker 1309. Adds `runtime.py notify --title --body` (desktop
`notify-send` where present, plus an alert file under the git common dir, rate
limited per condition, the pattern of the arena's `scripts/arena-watchdog.py`)
and decides on an out-of-session raid supervisor: a systemd user timer that runs
`raid-sitrep.py` and calls `notify` when the queue is not empty and no SITREP has
been written for 30 minutes (coordinator presumed dead). `notify` is also the
documented fallback whenever `can wake` answers no.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `notify` verb with a rate limit and a test (stubbed notify-send, alert file written)
- [ ] Decision recorded: build the supervisor or drop it, with raid-log evidence
      (as of 2026-10-28, 8 raids and no dead coordinator)
- [ ] If built: unit + timer installed by `bin/idh install`, documented in raid § Sitrep cadence
- [ ] `make check` passes
